  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The leaves have 9-13 lobes which are divided about halfway to the leaf base. Margins Acer maximowiczianum. are deeply toothed, giving a feather-edge appearance. The leaf surface is sometimes sparingly covered with fine, silvery hairs. Spring and summer colors are a deep, rich green, almost a bluegreen in partial shade. Fall color is outstanding with red, crimson, gold, and orange blends. This maple forms a small tree up to 13 ft. (4 m) tall. The name means \"big waterfall.\""
  },
